  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an integer `n`, output *a list of all **simplified** fractions between* `0` *and* `1` *(exclusive) such that the denominator is less-than-or-equal-to* `n`. You can output the answer in **any order**.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 2\nOutput: [\"1/2\"]\nExplanation: \"1/2\" is the only unique fraction with a denominator less-than-or-equal-to 2.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 3\nOutput: [\"1/2\",\"1/3\",\"2/3\"]\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 4\nOutput: [\"1/2\",\"1/3\",\"1/4\",\"2/3\",\"3/4\"]\nExplanation: \"2/4\" is not a simplified fraction because it can be simplified to \"1/2\".\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 100`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
